 The list of discovered PuppetDB targets is refreshed at the interval, which can be configured via `-promscrape.puppetdbSDCheckInterval` command-line flag.
 
+## scaleway_sd_configs
+
+Scaleway SD configuration allows retrieving scrape targets from [Scaleway's Instances API](https://www.scaleway.com/en/developers/api/instance/#path-servers-list-all-servers).
+
+Configuration example:
+
+```yaml
+scrape_configs:
+- job_name: scaleway
+  scaleway_sd_configs:
+
+    # zone is an optional Scaleway zone to discover instances in, e.g. "fr-par-1", "nl-ams-1" or "pl-waw-1".
+    # By default, "fr-par-1" is used.
+    # Add one scaleway_sd_configs entry per zone in order to discover instances in multiple zones.
+    #
+  - zone: "fr-par-1"
+
+    # project_id is an optional id of the Scaleway project to discover instances for.
+    #
+    # project_id: "..."
+
+    # organization_id is an optional id of the Scaleway organization to discover instances for.
+    #
+    # organization_id: "..."
+
+    # name_filter is an optional filter for discovered instances by name.
+    #
+    # name_filter: "..."
+
+    # tags_filter is an optional list of tags to filter discovered instances by.
+    # Only instances, which contain all the given tags, are discovered.
+    #
+    # tags_filter: ["...", "..."]
+
+    # server is an optional Scaleway API server to query.
+    # By default, https://api.scaleway.com is used.
+    #
+    # server: "https://api.scaleway.com"
+
+    # port is an optional port to scrape metrics from. By default, port 80 is used.
+    #
+    # port: ...
+
+    # The Scaleway secret key must be supplied as an API token via the usual HTTP API client options below,
+    # since Scaleway authenticates requests with the `X-Auth-Token` HTTP header instead of `Authorization: Bearer ...`.
+    #
+    headers: ["X-Auth-Token: <secret-key>"]
+
+    # Additional HTTP API client options can be specified here.
+    # See https://docs.victoriametrics.com/victoriametrics/sd_configs/#http-api-client-options
+```
+
+Each discovered target has an [`__address__`](https://docs.victoriametrics.com/victoriametrics/relabeling/#how-to-modify-scrape-urls-in-targets) label set
+to `<public_ipv4>:<port>`, where `<public_ipv4>` is the public IPv4 address of the instance (falling back to the private IPv4 address if the instance has no
+public IPv4 address), while `<port>` is the port specified in the `scaleway_sd_configs`.
+
+The following meta labels are available on discovered targets during [relabeling](https://docs.victoriametrics.com/victoriametrics/relabeling/):
+
+* `__meta_scaleway_instance_id`: the id of the instance
+* `__meta_scaleway_instance_name`: the name of the instance
+* `__meta_scaleway_instance_hostname`: the hostname of the instance
+* `__meta_scaleway_instance_boot_type`: the boot type of the instance
+* `__meta_scaleway_instance_image_id`: the id of the instance's image
+* `__meta_scaleway_instance_image_name`: the name of the instance's image
+* `__meta_scaleway_instance_organization_id`: the id of the organization the instance belongs to
+* `__meta_scaleway_instance_project_id`: the id of the project the instance belongs to
+* `__meta_scaleway_instance_private_ipv4`: the private IPv4 of the instance
+* `__meta_scaleway_instance_public_ipv4`: the public IPv4 of the instance
+* `__meta_scaleway_instance_public_ipv6`: the public IPv6 of the instance
+* `__meta_scaleway_instance_region`: the region of the instance, derived from its zone
+* `__meta_scaleway_instance_zone`: the zone of the instance
+* `__meta_scaleway_instance_security_group_id`: the id of the instance's security group
+* `__meta_scaleway_instance_security_group_name`: the name of the instance's security group
+* `__meta_scaleway_instance_status`: the status of the instance
+* `__meta_scaleway_instance_type`: the commercial type of the instance
+* `__meta_scaleway_instance_tags`: the comma-separated list of tags of the instance
+
+The list of discovered Scaleway targets is refreshed at the interval, which can be configured via `-promscrape.scalewaySDCheckInterval` command-line flag.
+
 ## static_configs
 
 A static config allows specifying a list of targets and a common label set for them.
